                    "message": "I'm in support of this experiment.  haven't reviewed the patch yet."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for looking into WIP patches and providing some initial feedback \ud83d\udc4d\n\nNow the patch is ready for review and some of the choices are\n\n- Do we install a wrapper script or a symlink instead\n- Do we generate the `libexec` path or is it fine to hardcode it\n- Do we still compile the cli separately (as test for now) to ensure it uses only the declared dependencies? (Tradeoff with compile time)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "If we're still asking questions, please don't close out the thread, it makes your questions hard to respond to.\n\n> Do we install a wrapper script or a symlink instead\n\nMinor preference for symlink here, just so we don't have to maintain a script, and there's no potential people add extra stuff to the script.\n\n> Do we generate the libexec path or is it fine to hardcode it\nGenerate based on the provided prefix please.\n\n> Do we still compile the cli separately \nNo, lets make sure the commit represents what we think the current state of the art is.  If we need to revert/pull things from history, we can always do that."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Minor preference for symlink here, just so we don't have to maintain a script, and there's no potential people add extra stuff to the script.\n\nGood points \ud83d\udc4d\n\nThanks for the precise and complete feedback."
                }
            ],
