                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Lets get this phrased not as an \"experiment\".  Lets get this phrased as why we're doing what we're doing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Reopening this.  Current patchset still says \"hypothesis\". If this merges, this isn't a hypothesis, this commit message is a conclusion, so lets document why this is better."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Ok, i removed the word `hypothesis` from all parts of the commit message.\n\n> so lets document why this is better.\n\nI outlined the commands used to check the resulting size.\n\nIt is better because we achieve a smaller footprint in compressed rofs.\n\nHow much is to gain by merging binaries depends on their contents and overlap. It depends on case-by-case basis. Sometimes the gain would be very small.\n\nDocumenting all the cases where it works and where it does not would be a bunch of work involving prepared example sources and going over compiler internals, how `-Osize` works, how it impacts inlining, how specialization/inlining with single caller can prevent deduplication later on, ...\n\n\nSo i don't see us covering all of that in a single commit message.\n\n\nCan we keep it at \"this is better, it makes sense that it's better, for details, go dig up compiler internals\" ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We don't need compiler level details.  \"This is better, here's the measurement, and here's the test results.  This makes sense because....\" is plenty.  The important part is we don't phrase this as an experiment.  If we merge it, it's canon.\n\nIn what you currently have I would also take out \"Conclusion: \" and replace \"Results: \" with \"Tested:\" per the commit message rules.\n\nWith that said, It's a commit message, I'm not that worried about it.  Lets just get this in."
                },
                {
                    "file": "scripts/target/bmcweb",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "remove."
