            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meson.build",
                    "line": 421,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Now that this is an application we expect people to execute, libexec isn't appropriate.  Move it back to bindir (same as the cli was)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.build",
                    "line": 421,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Ok, then we will not need a symlink anymore."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.build",
                    "line": 421,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Exactly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/webserver_cli.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "is there a way in CLI11 to keep the old behavior where launching with no args runs this daemon command?  There's lots of documentation that just expects bmcweb to launch on its own that it would be great to not break."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/webserver_cli.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Lets keep this sub command just so we can have help strings if we want."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/webserver_cli.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> There's lots of documentation that just expects bmcweb to launch on its own that it would be great to not break.\n\nyou mean `bmcweb` service?\n\nOtherwise, `bmcwebd` was a separate binary before this patch, so any docs that reference it will be outdated.\n\nI'm having trouble relating this comment to your other comment about putting the binary into bindir. Which gets rid of the symlink that was previously used.\n\n> Lets keep this sub command just so we can have help strings if we want.\n\nok, i will keep as is."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/webserver_cli.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "bmcwebd is a relatively new binary, so very likely most of the documentation still points to bmcweb.\n\nIs it possible to have the no-args default be daemonize?  That's the ask.  I'm not that worried about it, people will figure it out."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/webserver_cli.cpp",
                    "line": 82,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This needs to be if(sub->parsed()) right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/webserver_cli.cpp",
                    "line": 82,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, for consistency we can put each code path beneath its sub-command.\n\nThis enables easily adding further sub-commands in the future."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/webserver_main.cpp",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please keep this file and have it call into webserver_cli.cpp.\n\nThe main has to be compiled as the last unit, so keeping the main with \"nothing\" in it helps with compile times by a few seconds."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/webserver_main.cpp",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
